ng about their history and  their customs  and each race looked felt and sounded  distinct by the time you get to the  citadel in mass effect 1 and you see  them all interacting with each other  it feels like the melting pot of the  galaxy that it's supposed to be  which is why andromeda was such a  disappointment to me in that regard  because  you crash land in this brand new galaxy  and the first new exciting alien species  you meet  the first thing you do is shoot them  well the first thing they did was shoot  you  but whatever the angara were cool but  the fact that there were a bunch of  races missing for narrative reasons like  the quarian and the drill meant that  andromeda just didn't feel  as populated i know the quarian arc  stuff was meant to be for dlc that never  materialized but still  it was a disappointment and that's why i  really really hope that in a new mass  effect  we'll get to see more alien races  if we're talking about combat throughout  the games each has its highs and lows  there's a lot to be said about mass  effect 1's combat it was pretty clunky  but it did have those deep rpg routes  which i loved mass effect 2 was more of  a mix between action and rpg  you could easily issue commands to your  squad but general movement didn't feel  as smooth as it could have  mass effect 3 is fast frenetic every  class can use every weapon  and there's more of an emphasis on  combos it's probably my favorite of the  lot  andromeda felt a bit floaty to me and as  someone who was more of a methodical  player  being unable to control my squadmates  power usage and stuff  just wasn't it for me i didn't really  enjoy that i like having control  i would genuinely love to see mass  effect take a more dragon age approach  and let you directly control assuming  direct control  of your squad mates during fights i also  think that like  if you make the classes feel a bit more  distinct that would be really cool  because otherwise  you know you might pick a class that you  think sounds interesting but you're not  really enjoying after 20 hours or so i  know you can respec and everything but  that would really give it an element of  fun on the fly  switching and experimentation  i'd be interested to know how you all  feel about the more open world aspects  of mass effect andromeda because  upon replaying the game i've just found  out that i don't i don't particularly  enjoy it  and actually thinking back i don't think  i enjoyed the more open-world  parts of the original mass effect either  and it's not because i hate piloting the  mako i am a mako apologist  i don't mind that clunky old thing but  when you compare one to two and three  where the level design was way much more  straightforward  it's night and day because i'm not just  driving around looking at a compass at  the top of my screen like i am in  andromeda  hoping to find something interesting so  i'm not saying that i wouldn't like to  see an open world mass effect i  genuinely think that could be really  interesting if it was something  the scale of red dead 2 or skyrim  i just think that if you're gonna make a  mass effect game that's open world  it has to be packed with stuff that  justifies that size  so i'm not talking about dragon age  inquisition where i'm  you know collecting shards around the  hinterlands i can't do that  again if you're gonna make these levels  big and huge  there has to be stuff in there to  justify it  i can't collect shards again please  don't make me  this is an obvious one but it's a topic  that's definitely worth bringing up when  it comes to  mass effect javik being day one dlc  sucked he was an integral part of that  game  he should never have been carved out and  sold separately he should have just been  in it andromeda's case with quarian arc  is  similar but different obviously they  left that thread dangling because they  thought it was going to be in dlc and it  would be resolved that way  but that dlc was cancelled and th